{"reference":"Psalms 115","book":"Psalms","chapter":115,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Nearby Psalms","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The psalms surrounding this chapter belong to a collection that includes communal memories of sanctuary destruction and Babylonian exile, alongside thanksgiving for return, festival praise, meditation on Torah, and Songs of Ascents oriented toward worship. Numbering differs in some Greek and Latin Psalter traditions: Psalms 114 and 115 are combined there, so this psalm may appear as part of a differently numbered unit.","verse_refs":["Psalms 113:1-9","Psalms 114:1-8","Psalms 116:1-19","Psalms 117:1-2","Psalms 118:1-29"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_115_420d83c82ddce19d34c8d1ca"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}